# The client of {@ project_name @}

A Vue 3 application, served by the binary once built. `npm install`, then `npm run dev`
while you work, or `npm run build` for the binary to serve it. Nothing here is generated
a second time: every file is yours, the interface components included.

## Where the look lives

In one block. `src/assets/main.css` opens on a `@theme` block holding every token the
components consume — seven colours, a radius scale, one typeface. No component names a
colour. Rewriting that block rewrites the identity, and `/galerie` shows the result on all
fourteen components at once.

The components under `src/components/ui` come from shadcn-vue and were frozen here rather
than pulled from it: the manifest carries no dependency on the command that produced them,
and the theme that command imports from its own package is written out above. The price is
that an upstream fix does not reach you on its own.

## Three versions held one major back

The manifest pins three packages away from the latest stable. Each holds a verified
incompatibility, not caution — check the incompatibility is gone before raising any of
them.

- **`typescript`** — the 7 no longer publishes `typescript/lib/tsc`, which `vue-tsc`
  loads to wrap the compiler. `npm run typecheck` then stops on
  `ERR_PACKAGE_PATH_NOT_EXPORTED` before reading a line. The same note sits in
  `tsconfig.json`.
- **`@vueuse/core`** — `reka-ui`, which the components are built on, depends on `^14`.
  Asking for the 15 at the root leaves both copies in the tree, and so in the bundle.
- **`@vue/devtools-api`** — nothing imports it. It is a *non-optional* peer of Pinia 4;
  leaving it out would make the install depend on how the installer resolves peers.
